<title>SWITZERLAND: Oerlikon turns loss into profit in H1.</title>
<headline>Oerlikon turns loss into profit in H1.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net profit	     23		  vs 29 loss</p>
<p> Gross sales		    1,712	     vs 1,651</p>
<p> Operating result	     94		  vs 36</p>
<p> Cash flow			98		  vs 52</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name is Oerlikon-Buehrle Holding AG.  </p>
<p> Orders received		1,791	     vs 1,673</p>
<p> Net income per share, Sfr  2		   vs 2 loss</p>
<p> Net debt			 1,381	     vs 1,356</p>
<p> Financial income	     11		  vs 19</p>
<p> Financial expense	    44		  vs 63</p>
<p> Pre-tax income		 65		  vs 4 loss</p>
<p> Fixed assets investments   114		 vs 132</p>
<p> Employees, end-June	  16,365	    vs 17,658</p>
<p> Taxes			    42		  vs 25</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
